A||||1||Ross||Performance from stock exaust manifold.
Z||000000||Ross||04-25-99||09:45 AM||||There is a process the 5.0 boys have been using on the upper and lower intake manifolds on their fuel injected 302's. It's also been used on the heads,it's called the extrude hone process. What's involved is a substance similiar to thick tooth paste with an abrasive additive that's forced through the head ports, or the manifold pleniums(off the block of course).This ports and polishes the parts alowing for easear breathing. What if we do this to the exaust manifolds? The casting is thick enough to be ported with this process not only will it open up the pipes thy will be polished also. No need for expensive headers.           
Z||000001||Pretender||04-25-99||11:29 PM||||you might as well buy the headers....i heard that process was very expensive. even doing that to the factory manifolds wouldn't increase the hp like the headers would.
